WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:11.473
Election Day was coming up everywhere—even at my school.

2
00:00:12.414 --> 00:00:13.394
But I had a problem.

3
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:18.857
My two best friends were running for school president!

4
00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:22.239
I could only vote for one of them.

5
00:00:25.101 --> 00:00:26.281
Abby is really smart.

6
00:00:26.862 --> 00:00:27.962
She's my next-door neighbor.

7
00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:30.504
She moved here a couple years ago.

8
00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:34.957
Matt is really popular.

9
00:00:35.978 --> 00:00:37.379
I've known him since kindergarten.

10
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.361
We play on the same baseball team.

11
00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.145
I helped them make campaign posters to hang in the school hallways.

12
00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:50.147
Matt and Abby both said, "Vote for me!"

13
00:00:51.268 --> 00:00:53.530
But how could I choose between my best friends?

14
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.872
Ugh! I wished there was no election.

15
00:00:56.892 --> 00:00:59.834
"Why do we have to vote?"

16
00:01:00.274 --> 00:01:01.015
I asked Mrs.

17
00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:02.416
Hardy during social studies.

18
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.063
"Voting is a way for people to show their opinions," she explained.

19
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:11.825
"Then decisions can be made based on the majority."

20
00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.506
That didn't solve my problem.

21
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.829
I decided to ask my sister about voting.

22
00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:21.850
Becca turned 18 this year.

23
00:01:23.931 --> 00:01:26.753
She can vote in a real election for the first time.

24
00:01:26.773 --> 00:01:29.895
"I can't wait to vote," she said.

25
00:01:29.915 --> 00:01:31.776
"Voting is a privilege!"

26
00:01:32.996 --> 00:01:33.976
"Who are you voting for?"

27
00:01:34.477 --> 00:01:34.917
I asked.

28
00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:36.818
"I'm not telling you."

29
00:01:37.518 --> 00:01:38.978
She stuck her tongue out at me.

30
00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.319
"Voting is private.

31
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.960
That way people can feel free when they vote."

32
00:01:46.662 --> 00:01:49.243
Downstairs, Mom and Dad were stuffing envelopes.

33
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:54.425
They volunteer for Mayor Morgan's campaign.

34
00:01:55.645 --> 00:01:58.426
Even our front lawn is filled with campaign signs!

35
00:01:59.627 --> 00:02:02.508
Mom and Dad always say that elections are important.

36
00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:07.306
"We pay taxes to the government," said Mom.

37
00:02:08.347 --> 00:02:10.289
"So we should choose good leaders."

38
00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:12.811
"How do you know who to vote for?"

39
00:02:13.311 --> 00:02:13.772
I asked.

40
00:02:14.472 --> 00:02:15.853
"Well," said Dad.

41
00:02:16.574 --> 00:02:19.116
"You have to think hard and know the facts."

42
00:02:21.398 --> 00:02:24.280
"Voting isn't just marking a ballot," added Mom.

43
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.302
"It's a serious responsibility.

44
00:02:27.963 --> 00:02:30.705
I vote for people who will make the world better for us."

45
00:02:32.106 --> 00:02:34.168
My parents didn't solve my problem.

46
00:02:35.308 --> 00:02:36.409
But they had good advice.

47
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.251
I thought really hard about who to vote for.

48
00:02:44.254 --> 00:02:46.075
Abby wanted new classroom computers.

49
00:02:47.316 --> 00:02:49.097
Matt wanted to fix the baseball field.

50
00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:51.819
They both had good ideas.

51
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.982
It wasn't easy, but finally I made a decision.

52
00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:00.645
This morning at school, we voted.

53
00:03:02.887 --> 00:03:04.568
But I'm not saying who I voted for.

54
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.662
Like Becca said, voting is private.

55
00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:11.505
The principal will announce the winner tomorrow.

56
00:03:12.586 --> 00:03:16.169
I know that he—or she!—will be a great school president.

57
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.331
I'm glad I answered my election question.

58
00:03:23.895 --> 00:03:25.997
But now I have a new problem!

59
00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:30.541
How will I cheer up the friend who doesn't win?

60
00:03:30.561 --> 00:03:32.843
Oh no!
